<title>MONGOLIA: Mongolia industrial ouput down 25.6 pct in '96.</title>
<headline>Mongolia industrial ouput down 25.6 pct in '96.</headline>
<dateline>ULAN BATOR 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mongolia's gross industrial output in 1996 fell by 25.6 percent to 239.27 billion tugriks, down from 321.66 billion tugriks in 1995, the State Statistics Centre said on Monday.</p>
<p>Major income from sales in 1996 came from the non-ferrous metals industry, with 123.67 billion tugriks, down from 136.06 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>($1.0=693 tugriks)</p>
</text>
